                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I mean the writing was alright. However it wasn't a lot of romance. For a dating game you would expect each character to have their own \"chapter\" or \"route\" but all of this was common route with differences based on your choices. Not romantic ones, mostly, mind you. There were differences in ending scenes and compared to the rest of the game it was a miniscule moment?\n\nOther than that, I liked the minigames BUT after a while they started to drag on when I wanted to see development with the characters. It broke the pace of the story. It also frustrated me a bit that you couldn't complete the journal in one playthrough - seems like an oversight tbh, and that it didn't save the entries anywhere so you could read it anytime you want.\n\nI liked it but it wasn't the best, and when it comes to dragging - I know how annoying it is, I'm a completionist and the common route was getting annoying at the end. It was just constant skipping with a little new dialogue. As opposed to them having their own route and maybe (I say it with the grain of salt cause it happens sometimes a bit of branching at the ending chapters/route when a new story appears? the bad/friendship/etc).I would give it a mixed review if I could but on the positive side (even though I mostly complained) I liked the story and the friendship that formed with the characters. And the fact that they have influence over other characters so they are more grounded in the story.",
